---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import results from "../data/results.json";

const suites = (results.suites ?? {}) as Record<string, any>;

// Compute table rows in frontmatter — conditional bare <tr> expressions break
// Astro's HTML compiler (table elements get hoisted out of expressions).
const srcFor = (name: string) =>
  name === "classification"
    ? "ag_news (HF)"
    : name === "routing"
      ? "customer-support-tickets (HF)"
      : name === "moderation"
        ? "tweet_eval/hate (HF)"
        : "synthetic (seeded)";
const suiteRows = Object.entries(suites).map(([name, s]: [string, any]) => ({
  name,
  n: s.n_items,
  src: srcFor(name),
  task: `${s.n_answers}-way choice`,
}));
const suiteRowsShown =
  suiteRows.length > 0
    ? suiteRows
    : [{ name: "classification", n: 200, src: "ag_news (HF)", task: "4-way choice" }];
---

<Base title="Methodology — Verdict">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="tagline">
    Verdict measures decision APIs on the same prompt, the same labeled items, and the same contract:
    <em>given a question with a finite set of allowed answers and some context, choose exactly one answer</em>.
    Everything on this site is reproducible from the repository with two commands.
  </p>

  <h2>The contract every provider must satisfy</h2>
  <pre><code>{`DecisionRequest:
  question:  str                  # the judgment to make
  answers:   list[str]            # finite, predefined answer set (verbatim choice required)
  context:   str | None           # text to judge

DecisionResponse:
  answer:      str | None         # must be one of the allowed answers
  confidence:  float | None       # 0..1, optional
  latency_ms, cost_usd            # measured per call`}</code></pre>
  <p class="tagline">
    All providers receive an identical system prompt and user prompt. Structured-output providers get a
    strict JSON schema (<code>answer</code> enum + <code>confidence</code>); providers without schema
    support (e.g. <code>jev-router</code> advertises no supported parameters) receive the same prompt as
    plain text and their answer is extracted by a shared robust parser (embedded JSON → exact match →
    quoted match → word-overlap fallback).
  </p>

  <h2>Suites</h2>
  <p class="tagline">Fixed, seeded, versioned JSONL files shipped inside the package. Real data wherever a public labeled source was available:</p>
  <table class="board">
    <thead><tr><th>Suite</th><th>Items</th><th>Source</th><th>Task</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {suiteRowsShown.map((r: any) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{r.name.replace("_", " ")}</td>
          <td class="num">{r.n}</td>
          <td class="num">{r.src}</td>
          <td class="num">{r.task}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Metrics</h2>
  <ul class="tagline">
    <li><strong>Accuracy</strong> — exact verbatim match against the labeled answer, over non-errored items.</li>
    <li><strong>Latency p50/p95</strong> — wall-clock per call measured in the client (network included), sequential-by-default; the published run uses concurrency 4 (mild queueing possible at p95).</li>
    <li><strong>Cost per 1,000 decisions</strong> — OpenRouter providers are billed at the authoritative per-generation amount returned by OpenRouter's <code>/generation</code> endpoint. OpenAI prices are our estimates (flagged in the harness) until confirmed against published pricing.</li>
    <li><strong>ECE</strong> — expected calibration error over 10 equal-width confidence bins; lower means the stated confidence is more honest. Computed only over items that reported confidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Escalation curves</strong> — offline simulation: items below a confidence threshold are "answered" by the escalation provider's already-recorded output (GPT-6 Luna by default), and we report blended accuracy and cost. No extra API calls are involved.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disclosed caveats</h2>
  <ul class="tagline">
    <li><strong>Proxy labeling.</strong> The OpenAI Decisions API is in limited preview and not enabled for our key at measurement time. Any provider labeled <span class="badge proxy">proxy</span> implements the same contract on a standard chat model — it is <em>not</em> the real Decisions API. When access lands, the real adapter runs in the same slot and the badge disappears.</li>
    <li><strong>jev-router opacity.</strong> Jev is a router: it picks an underlying model per request, and its listing price is unpublished. We report the charged amount per call and record the routed model.</li>
    <li><strong>Confidence comparability.</strong> Some providers return no confidence (excluded from ECE); others derive it from free text. Treat ECE as provider-internal honesty, not cross-provider gospel.</li>
    <li><strong>Snapshot pricing.</strong> Provider prices change; the cost table is dated and versioned in the repo (<code>cost.py</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Single-run variance.</strong> Temperature is 0 where supported, but routed providers can still vary. Nightly reruns smooth this out over time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reproduce it</h2>
  <pre><code>{`cd python
uv sync --extra dev
uv run python scripts/build_datasets.py   # rebuild suites (seeded)
uv run verdict bench --all --out ../results
uv run verdict aggregate --results ../results --out ../site/src/data/results.json
cd ../site && npm run build               # static site from real data`}</code></pre>
</Base>
